# React Router 7 Forms

`<Form>` from `react-router` routes the submission through the matched route's `action`, supports pending UI, and avoids a full document navigation. A plain `<form>` does a full page reload and never reaches the route action.

## Basic mutation

```tsx
import { Form } from "react-router";
import type { Route } from "./+types/contact";
import { z } from "zod";
import { data } from "react-router";

const ContactSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
  message: z.string().min(1),
});

export async function action({ request }: Route.ActionArgs) {
  const form = await request.formData();
  const parsed = ContactSchema.safeParse(Object.fromEntries(form));
  if (!parsed.success) {
    return data({ fieldErrors: parsed.error.flatten().fieldErrors }, { status: 400 });
  }
  await sendMessage(parsed.data);
  return { ok: true };
}

export default function Contact({ actionData }: Route.ComponentProps) {
  return (
    <Form method="post">
      <label>
        Email
        <input name="email" type="email" required />
        {actionData && "fieldErrors" in actionData && actionData.fieldErrors.email && (
          <p role="alert">{actionData.fieldErrors.email[0]}</p>
        )}
      </label>
      <label>
        Message
        <textarea name="message" required />
      </label>
      <button type="submit">Send</button>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

## fetcher.Form

In-page mutation without changing URL or navigating. Useful for "Add to cart", "Toggle favourite", inline edits.

```tsx
import { useFetcher } from "react-router";
function AddToCart({ id }: { id: string }) {
  const fetcher = useFetcher({ key: `add-${id}` });
  const pending = fetcher.state !== "idle";
  return (
    <fetcher.Form method="post" action="/cart/add">
      <input type="hidden" name="productId" value={id} />
      <button disabled={pending} type="submit">{pending ? "Adding..." : "Add"}</button>
    </fetcher.Form>
  );
}
```

When rendering many fetchers in a list, pass a unique `key` per fetcher; otherwise they share one slot and submissions stomp.

## useFormAction

Resolves the current route's URL so the action path tracks file renames.

```tsx
import { Form, useFormAction } from "react-router";
function EditForm() {
  const action = useFormAction();
  return <Form method="post" action={action}>{/* ... */}</Form>;
}
```

## Multipart uploads

```tsx
<Form method="post" encType="multipart/form-data">
  <input type="file" name="avatar" />
  <button type="submit">Upload</button>
</Form>
```

On the server, parse with `request.formData()` (built-in) or a stream parser for large files.

## Refused patterns

- Plain `<form method="post">` for a route action. Triggers a full reload.
- A mutation `<Form action="/x">` without `method="post"`. Defaults to GET, which runs the loader, not the action. Search and filter forms are the exception: GET is intentional, the URL is the canonical state.
- `useFetcher()` (no key) inside a `.map()`. All fetchers share one slot.

